# The design-sync durable set must stay LF on every platform.
#
# The converter embeds these files verbatim into the uploaded artifacts:
# previews/*.tsx snippets go into each component's .prompt.md, and
# conventions.md is prepended to the generated README. With Windows'
# core.autocrlf=true they check out as CRLF, so a sync run on Windows rewrites
# ~35 .prompt.md files with no text change — and the next run on macOS rewrites
# them back. Pinning LF stops that ping-pong.
.design-sync/** text eol=lf
